    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1245">

                <pb facs="0868" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/380.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Bevan to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Colonel Nafarrate, chief military official in Tampico, called on this office this
                    evening and advised that all the business houses in Tampico would be forced to
                    pay a war tax regardless of nationality. He laid stress on the fact that it was
                    the business that was being taxed and not the owners of the business. I
                    requested that he give the list of American and Spanish firms and the amounts
                    assessed before trying <pb facs="0869" n="753" xml:id="pg753"/> to collect same
                    which he agreed to do. He also agreed to allow me seventy-two hours in which to
                    place the matter before the Department for instructions before he would force
                    the payment. Most of the firms have expressed their willingness to abide by the
                    advice of this office regard to payment, will advise Department fully as soon as
                    lists are received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bevan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
